    "id": "fef3d10918b05446d917611d",
    "path": "datafusion_expr_common::statistics::ExponentialDistribution",
    "name": "ExponentialDistribution",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "datafusion-expr-common",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct ExponentialDistribution",
    "docs": "Exponential distribution with an optional shift. The probability density\nfunction (PDF) is defined as follows:\n\nFor a positive tail (when `positive_tail` is `true`):\n\n`f(x; λ, offset) = λ exp(-λ (x - offset))    for x ≥ offset`\n\nFor a negative tail (when `positive_tail` is `false`):\n\n`f(x; λ, offset) = λ exp(-λ (offset - x))    for x ≤ offset`\n\n\nIn both cases, the PDF is `0` outside the specified domain.\n\nFor more information, see:\n\n<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_distribution>",
